+      matches:
+        - '\b(?:FieldFragment|FieldScope|ScopeFacts)\b'
+        - '(?:import|export)\s+(?:type\s+)?\{[^}]*\b(?:Fragment|Scope)\b[^}]*\}\s*from\s*[''"]@(?:prisma/[\w-]+/orm-client|internal/sql-orm-client)[''"]'
+        - 'import\s+(?:type\s+)?\*\s+as\s+([\w$]+)\s+from\s*[''"]@(?:prisma/[\w-]+/orm-client|internal/sql-orm-client)[''"][\s\S]*\b\1\.(?:Fragment|Scope)\b'
+        - 'import\(\s*[''"]@(?:prisma/[\w-]+/orm-client|internal/sql-orm-client)[''"]\s*\)\.(?:Fragment|FieldFragment|Scope|FieldScope)\b'
+  - id: unique-criterion-rejects-null
+    summary: |
+      `UniqueConstraintCriterion` in the SQL ORM client (`@prisma/orm-postgres/orm-client`, the other facades' `orm-client` entries and `@internal/sql-orm-client`) no longer accepts `null` for a nullable unique column, so the `conflictOn` of `upsert` and the criteria of a relation `connect` or `disconnect` stop compiling when a value is `null` or may be `null`. Pass a non-null value, or handle the null case before the call. The detection matches every `conflictOn`, `.connect(` and `.disconnect(`; leave as they are the calls on other objects, such as `postgres.connect(...)`, and the `conflictOn` of `createAll` and `createAndCount`, which is an array of field names.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bconflictOn\b|\.(?:connect|disconnect)\s*\(|\bUniqueConstraintCriterion\b'
+  - id: prepared-all-and-aggregate-need-their-receiver
+    summary: |
+      On every collection of the SQL ORM client, `prepared.all` and `prepared.aggregate` no longer compile when called without the `prepared` object as their receiver, such as after `const { all } = collection.prepared`. Call them on the `prepared` object. `prepared.first` and `prepared.firstOrThrow` are not affected, and nothing changes at run time.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - '\{[^}]*\b(?:all|aggregate)\b[^}]*\}\s*=\s*[^;\n]*\.prepared\b'
+  - id: build-native-enums-takes-the-domain
+    summary: |
+      `buildNamespacedNativeEnums` from `@prisma/orm-postgres/runtime` takes the contract's domain as a second argument, `buildNamespacedNativeEnums(contract.storage, contract.domain)`, and leaves out each value set that a domain enum of the same namespace produced. The accessors it builds hold native enum types only; read a domain enum through the accessor `db.enums` uses.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bbuildNamespacedNativeEnums\s*\('
+  - id: middleware-hooks-are-activity-hooks
+    summary: |
+      The per-statement middleware hooks are replaced. `beforeQuery` and `beforeExecute` become `beforeEncode`; `interceptQuery` and `interceptExecute` become `intercept.onQuery` and `intercept.onExecute`; `afterQuery` and `afterExecute` become `activityEnded` on a statement; `afterTransaction` becomes `activityFinalized` on a statement. `onRow` and `beforeCompile` are unchanged.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\b(beforeQuery|beforeExecute|interceptQuery|interceptExecute|afterQuery|afterExecute|afterTransaction)\b'
+  - id: middleware-context-is-activity-context
+    summary: |
+      `RuntimeMiddlewareContext` is renamed `ActivityContext`. It gains `parent`, `state(key)` and `inTransaction()`, and loses `planExecutionId`; use `activity.id` instead.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bRuntimeMiddlewareContext\b'
+        - '\bplanExecutionId\b'
+  - id: after-result-types-removed
+    summary: |
+      `AfterQueryResult`, `AfterExecuteResult` and `AfterTransactionResult` are removed. Use `ActivityEndedResult` (narrow it with `result.kind === 'statement'` and `result.returns`) and `ActivityFinalizedResult`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bAfter(Query|Execute|Transaction)Result\b'
+  - id: aborted-phase-before-encode
+    summary: |
+      A `RUNTIME.ABORTED` error raised during the middleware stage before encoding reports `details.phase: 'beforeEncode'`, not `'beforeQuery'` or `'beforeExecute'`. The phases `'afterQuery'` and `'afterExecute'` no longer occur. Mongo's `RUNTIME.CONTENT_HASH_REQUIRES_RESOLVED_COMMAND` also reports `details.phase: 'beforeEncode'`, not `'beforeExecute'`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '[''"`](beforeQuery|beforeExecute|afterQuery|afterExecute)[''"`]'
+  - id: every-started-statement-is-ended-and-finalized
+    summary: |
+      Every statement the runtime accepts now starts an activity, and every started statement ends and is finalized exactly once. A call with an already-aborted signal fires `activityStarted` before it fails. A statement that fails before it runs, in `beforeCompile`, `beforeEncode` or parameter encoding, now ends `failed` and is finalized, where it got no `afterTransaction` before. `activityEnded` also fires for a statement the caller stopped reading (outcome `'stopped'`) and for a statement that failed before it ran (outcome `'failed'`, `latencyMs: 0`, `source: 'driver'`); `afterQuery` and `afterExecute` fired for neither, so a metrics or slow-query middleware now counts them unless it checks `result.outcome`. When a middleware's `activityStarted` throws, the middleware after it receive no `activityEnded` or `activityFinalized` for that activity. A statement still running when its transaction ends, such as a row stream still being read, is finalized when it ends, with the transaction's outcome, and keeps its `ctx.state` until then.
+  - id: observed-row-budget-runs
+    summary: |
+      The `budgets()` middleware now counts the rows a query returns and enforces `maxRows` on them. Before, the observed-row check never ran. With the default row severity `'error'`, or in `strict` mode, a query that returns more than `maxRows` rows fails with `BUDGET.ROWS_EXCEEDED`; with `'warn'` in `permissive` mode it logs one warning for the statement and keeps streaming.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bbudgets\('
+  - id: statement-runners-replace-middleware-runners
+    summary: |
+      `runBeforeQueryChain`, `runBeforeExecuteChain`, `runQueryWithMiddleware`, `runExecuteWithMiddleware`, `runAfterTransaction`, `reportQueryEnding`, `reportExecuteEnding`, `onQueryEndOutsideTransaction` and `QueryEnding` are removed from `@prisma/orm-framework`. A runtime runs a statement with `streamStatement` or `executeStatement`, whose body calls `beforeEncode`, `runQuery` and `runExecute`, and opens a transaction with `startTransactionActivity`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\b(runBeforeQueryChain|runBeforeExecuteChain|runQueryWithMiddleware|runExecuteWithMiddleware|runAfterTransaction|reportQueryEnding|reportExecuteEnding|onQueryEndOutsideTransaction|QueryEnding|afterTransactionStageFor|anyMiddlewareDeclaresAfterTransaction)\b'
+  - id: runtime-core-context-fields
+    summary: |
+      `RuntimeCoreOptions.ctx` is an `ActivityContextFields`: the context fields without `parent`, `state` and `inTransaction`, and without `planExecutionId`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bplanExecutionId\s*:'
+  - id: begin-transaction-on
+    summary: |
+      `SqlRuntimeBase.wrapTransaction(driverTx, connection)` is replaced by `beginTransactionOn(connection, owner)`, which starts the transaction activity, runs `BEGIN` on the connection and returns the wrapped transaction. `owner` is the `RuntimeConnection` the subclass hands to its callers for that connection; when the transaction's `activityStarted` hooks refuse the start before `BEGIN`, `withTransaction` releases `owner`, and after any other start failure it destroys it.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - '\bwrapTransaction\s*\('
+  - id: middleware-debug-events-renamed
+    summary: |
+      The runtime's debug events `middleware.interceptQuery` and `middleware.interceptExecute` are now `middleware.intercept.onQuery` and `middleware.intercept.onExecute`, and the logged error event `middleware.afterTransaction.error` is now `middleware.activityFinalized.error`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts,tsx}"
+      matches:
+        - 'middleware\.(interceptQuery|interceptExecute|afterTransaction\.error)'
+  - id: rename-statements-capability-removed
+    summary: |
+      `TargetMigrationsCapability.renameStatements` (with `refused` and `keepDataByHand`), added in 8.0.0-rc.17, is removed: every target's planner carries out rename statements. The CLI no longer appends a target's text to a data-loss question.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - '(?<![\w$])(?:renameStatements|keepDataByHand)\s*:'
+  - id: mongo-ddl-rename-collection
+    summary: |
+      `MongoDdlCommandVisitor` gains `renameCollection(command: RenameCollectionCommand)`, and `AnyMongoDdlCommand` and `AnyMongoDdlWireCommand` gain `RenameCollectionCommand` and `RenameCollectionWireCommand` (source in `collection`, new name in `to`). A visitor implementation, or a driver's `run`, handles the new kind.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - '(?<![\w$])(?:MongoDdlCommandVisitor|AnyMongoDdlCommand|AnyMongoDdlWireCommand)(?![\w$])'
+  - id: mongo-dml-operations
+    summary: |
+      `MongoDataTransformOperation` is renamed `MongoDmlOperation`, and `MongoDataTransformCheck` `MongoDmlCheck`. Its `operationClass` is any `MigrationOperationClass`, not only `'data'`: the planner's document rewrites (`renameField`, `unsetField`) are DML operations with class `widening` or `destructive`. Tell a DML operation from a DDL operation with `isMongoDmlOperation(operation)` (it has `run`), not with `operationClass === 'data'`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - 'operationClass\s*===?\s*["'']data["'']'
+        - '(?<![\w$])MongoDataTransform(?:Operation|Check)(?![\w$])'
+  - id: mongo-update-many-bypass-validation
+    summary: |
+      `RawUpdateManyCommand` takes an optional fourth argument `{ bypassDocumentValidation }`; `UpdateManyWireCommand` takes it as an optional fifth constructor argument and carries `bypassDocumentValidation: boolean`; the lowered `rawUpdateMany` draft (`MongoLoweredDraft`) requires `bypassDocumentValidation: boolean`.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - 'kind:\s*["'']rawUpdateMany["'']'
+  - id: mongo-op-factory-call-to-op
+    summary: |
+      A Mongo `OpFactoryCall`'s `toOp()`, and `renderOps(calls)`, return `AnyMongoMigrationOperation`, since `RenameFieldCall` and `UnsetFieldCall` produce DML operations.
+    detection:
+      glob: "**/*.{ts,mts,cts}"
+      matches:
+        - '["'']@(?:prisma/orm-target-mongo|internal/target-mongo)(?:/[^"'']*)?["''][\s\S]*(?:\.toOp\(\)|(?<![\w$])renderOps\s*\()'
